{
  "dom_id": "question-314884",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14212968/assets/bf0aa0508025b800bb0707b74ffdc89b08052ad6fced401b8071d7ad741f8e0a.png)\n\nA lighthouse $L$ shines a beam that hits the surface of the sea at point $B.$ The light is mounted at a height of $10\\,\\text{m}$ above the water. As the beam is tilted downward, the angle of elevation $\\theta $ made by the beam and the point $B$ is increasing at a rate of $0.12$ radians per second. What is the speed of the light spot as a function of $\\theta ?$ \n\n*Hint*: Remember that speed is always positive or zero.\n\nThe speed of the light spot is \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}.$",
